From c680b4e3c84dfaef0081fb8d87c4e90e0159f4f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elliotttate <elliotttate@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 01:09:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] gxcore: a fast path for the vertex decode

build_draw_plan_into's vertex loop interprets the walk for every element
of every vertex: the entry's kind, its index width, the format of each
component, the array lookup and the payload bounds, each a branch. It
was the largest part of the GX worker's busy time at the sea (about 30
percent, 2026-10-05). decode_vertices_fast first reduces each entry to
an op (format and component count in one code, the array's base,
stride and last valid offset), checks the payload's size once for the
draw, and decodes with the same expressions, so the same floats. A draw
it does not take (normal+binormal+tangent, an unknown format, an
unresolved array, a short payload) or an index outside its array's
bounds goes to the interpreting loop, which decodes it as before, with
its counters. DOL_GXCORE_FAST_DECODE=0 leaves every draw to that loop;
=verify decodes each draw both ways and reports a difference.

gxcore_tests pass with it on, off and verifying (no difference); a tour
of nine places verifying found only a skinned mesh the game rewrote
between the two decodes. Smooth Motion dumps at six places: real and
in-between frames identical.
